@* Written in each component, not in an _Imports.razor, whose class Razor makes public (ADR-0201).
   Every product using is written with global::. The component lives in ExPivot.Components, where a
   plain "ExPivot.Engine" could be looked up against the ExPivot component class first, and a plain
   "ExGrid.X" against sibling types (the CS0426 trap in AGENTS.md). The Web namespace makes @on...
   handlers compile as event handlers rather than as plain HTML attributes. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::ExGrid
@using global::ExGrid.Cells
@using global::ExGrid.Chrome
@using global::ExGrid.Columns
@using global::ExGrid.Components
@using global::ExGrid.Rows
@using global::ExGrid.Selection
@using global::ExPivot.Chrome
@using global::ExPivot.Engine
@* Not the contract (ADR-0201): ExPivot renders this as the Pivot Toolbar when the Pivot Chrome
   draws none, and no Consumer places it. It is public only because Razor makes every component
   public, is hidden from a Consumer's editor, and may change in any version. *@
@attribute [System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsable(System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsableState.Never)]
@* The built-in Pivot Toolbar above the report (ADR-0061): the report filter band on its left, and
   on its right, in this order, Layout ▾, Refresh when the source can be refreshed, and the Field
   List's toggle. Layout ▾'s wrapper is positioned, so the menu opens under it, over the report, at
   its right edge. Under the Pivot Toolbar, what the report could not do with the last change
   is said. Every button claims its input, in the pivot's Input Order (ADR-0240 section 6). *@
<div class="ex-pivot-toolbar">
    <div class="ex-pivot-toolbar-start">@Context.ReportFilters</div>
    <div class="ex-pivot-toolbar-end">
        <span class="ex-pivot-toolbar-anchor">
            <PivotFocusButton Class="ex-pivot-toolbar-button ex-pivot-layout-button" OnClick="Context.LayoutMenu.Open"
                              FocusRequest="Context.LayoutMenu.FocusRequest" aria-haspopup="menu"
                              aria-expanded="@(Context.LayoutMenu.IsOpen ? "true" : "false")">
                <span>@Context.LayoutMenu.Label</span>
                <span class="ex-pivot-entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
            </PivotFocusButton>
            @Context.LayoutMenu.Popup
        </span>
        @if (Context.Refresh is { } refresh)
        {
            <PivotFocusButton Class="ex-pivot-toolbar-button ex-pivot-refresh-button" Disabled="!refresh.Enabled"
                              OnClick="refresh.Invoke">@refresh.Label</PivotFocusButton>
        }
        <PivotFocusButton Class="ex-pivot-toolbar-button ex-pivot-field-list-toggle"
                          aria-pressed="@(Context.FieldList.Checked == true ? "true" : "false")"
                          OnClick="Context.FieldList.Invoke">@Context.FieldList.Label</PivotFocusButton>
    </div>
</div>
@if (Context.Refusal is { } refusal)
{
    <div class="ex-pivot-refusal-notice" role="alert">@refusal</div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>What to draw and whom to call back (ADR-0061).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public PivotToolbarContext Context { get; set; } = default!;
}
